meta {
  name: Get Removal Impact
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:id/removal-impact
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~deletedPipelineIds: {{pipelineId}}
  ~removedLinks: {{pipelineId}}:{{dataSinkId}}
  ~deletedDataSinkIds: {{dataSinkId}}
}

params:path {
  id: {{dataSetId}}
}

tests {
  test("Status code is 200", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("Impact lists DataSinks, Layers and APIs", function() {
    expect(res.body.dataSinks).to.be.an('array');
    expect(res.body.layers).to.be.an('array');
    expect(res.body.apis).to.be.an('array');
  });
  test("An empty request removes nothing", function() {
    expect(res.body.dataSinks).to.have.lengthOf(0);
    expect(res.body.layers).to.have.lengthOf(0);
    expect(res.body.apis).to.have.lengthOf(0);
    expect(res.body.requiresConfirmation).to.equal(false);
  });
}

docs {
  **Read-only preview** of what a Pipeline delete, a Pipeline update or a DataSink delete would remove. Requires `DATASET_READ`.

  | Query parameter (repeatable, optional) | Change to preview |
  |---|---|
  | `deletedPipelineIds=<pipelineId>` | `DELETE /datasets/{id}/pipelines/{pipelineId}` |
  | `removedLinks=<pipelineId>:<dataSinkId>` | a Pipeline `PUT`/`PATCH` whose `dataSinkIds` no longer lists the DataSink |
  | `deletedDataSinkIds=<dataSinkId>` | `DELETE /datasets/{id}/datasinks/{dataSinkId}` |

  The impact is calculated on the state after all given changes together, so one call covers a save that changes several Pipelines. An id that does not belong to the DataSet answers `404`. A `deletedDataSinkIds` entry that a Pipeline still links after the given changes answers `409` with type `urn:civitas:error:RESOURCE_IN_USE`: remove the DataSink from its Pipelines first.

  The response lists the DataSinks that become inactive (`id`, `dataSinkType`, `provisioned`), the Layers that go (`id`, `layerName`, `title`) and the APIs that go (`id`, `slug`, `name`, `standard`). `requiresConfirmation` is `true` when a provisioned DataSink, a Layer or an API goes. The mutation then needs the ids of all of these in `confirmedRemovalIds`, otherwise it answers `409` `REMOVAL_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED`.

  This request sends no change, so the impact is empty. Enable the query parameters to preview a change; `dataset-saga-workflow` step 14c previews a Pipeline delete with a non-empty impact.

  **Precondition:** `dataSetId` is set.

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK, body `{ "dataSinks": [], "layers": [], "apis": [], "requiresConfirmation": false }`.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | — (read-only) |
  | Config Adapter | — |
  | External System | — |
}
